eetings From Costa Rica!"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Present Continuous vs. Be Going To"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> and <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span> to talk about future actions and events. <br><Br>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to talk about arrangements and plans. <span class=\"strong\">Be going to</span> puts an emphasis on the idea of intention (decide to do something). <br><br>Example: <span class=\"italic\">I'm meeting with the tour group this afternoon. <span class=\"strong\">vs.</span> I'm going to meet the guide this week. </span> <br><br> You can use <span class=\"strong\">intend to</span> in place of <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm visiting a restaurant. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm checking out the wine bar."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm going to go to the museum today."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are you going sightseeing today?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I intend to go on a walk."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "old "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that exists for a long time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Paris is an old city."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about Paris."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "art"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "paintings, drawings"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There's great art in the museums."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "window-shopping"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the activity of looking at goods in shop windows without intending to buy them"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to go window-shopping for clothing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "designer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who makes plans or patterns for clothes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Many designers work in Paris."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to intend"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have something in your mind "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I intend on visiting these shops."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wine bar"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small restaurant where wine is the main drink available"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to check out a wine bar in Paris."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sweet tooth"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who enjoys eating sweet food "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Paris is any sweet tooth's dream!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to drool "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to let saliva come out of your mouth"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm drooling just thinking about all these desserts!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "macaroon"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small round cake"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Paris is famous for its macaroons."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le01ob03aud09"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le01ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a city."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go on the internet. Find places and things to do in this city."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 3 sentences about where you intend to go."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 3 sentences about what you plan to do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 3 sentences starting with <span class=\"italic\">I'm going to ...</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your sentences aloud to your class."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about my plans and intentions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the Present Continuous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use <span class=\"italic\">Going to</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my sentences aloud."}]}], "type": "sena"}